<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rastatt Palace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1700–1707</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rastatt">Rastatt</a> Palace is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> residence in Rastatt, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, built from 1700 for Margrave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-william-margrave-of-baden-baden">Louis William of Baden-Baden</a> after French troops burned Baden-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> in 1689. Modelled on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a>, it was the first Baroque palace of its kind on the Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-rastatt">Treaty of Rastatt</a> of 1714 and the Congress of Rastatt of 1797 to 1799 took place there.</p></div>
